    "summary": "USB-C is a physical connector standard, while Thunderbolt is a high-performance data protocol that uses the USB-C connector. Though they look identical, Thunderbolt offers significantly greater bandwidth, PCIe support, and daisy-chaining capabilities that matter most to power users and professionals.",
